WIRE.md §4.1, TYPES.md §1: a `@json(pairs:)` element has two present scalar fields; an optional field is not one, whether its type is `Int?` or the error type made optional (`Nope?`), so both are E3316 (the error type is a wildcard only where it stands).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record IntOpt {
  k: Int
  v: Int?
}

local record TwoOpt {
  k: Int
  v: Nope?
}

local record R {
  a: [IntOpt](..=3) = [] @json(pairs: ["a{i}", "b{i}"])
  b: [TwoOpt](..=3) = [] @json(pairs: ["c{i}", "d{i}"])
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2102]  a/a.canon:10:6
  unknown name Nope

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:14:26
  @json(pairs) does not apply to [a.IntOpt](..=3)

error[E3316]  a/a.canon:15:26
  @json(pairs) does not apply to [a.TwoOpt](..=3)

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
